.PP
Creates a FlexSpan view over the entire Array starting at index 0\&. The view uses the specified indexing mode (System, Reverse, Ring) and provides a span-like interface backed directly by this Array\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvector\fP \fBReference\fP to the Array\&. Passed by ref to avoid copying the struct and to ensure the FlexSpan reflects the actual container\&. 
.br
\fImode\fP Indexing mode for the view: System = forward indexing, Reverse = backward indexing, Ring = circular wrap-around indexing\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A FlexSpan representing the full Array\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Definition at line \fB281\fP of file \fBFixedVector\&.cs\fP\&.
.SS "VectorFlexSpan< T, \fBFixedVector\fP< T > > SystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.FixedVector< T >\&.AsFlexSpan (ref \fBFixedVector\fP< T > vector, long start, long end, \fBFlexSpanMode\fP mode = \fR\fBFlexSpanMode::System\fP\fP)\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Creates a FlexSpan view over a specific range of the Array\&. The view covers the range [start \&.\&. end) and uses the specified indexing mode\&. No memory is allocated; this is a pure logical slice backed by the Array\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvector\fP \fBReference\fP to the Array\&. Passed by ref so the FlexSpan operates on the actual container rather than a copy\&. 
.br
\fIstart\fP Starting index of the view\&. Must be within the Array's logical bounds\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP Exclusive end index of the view\&. Must be greater than or equal to start and within the Array's logical bounds\&. 
.br
\fImode\fP Indexing mode for the view: System = forward indexing, Reverse = backward indexing, Ring = circular wrap-around indexing\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A FlexSpan representing the specified range of the Array\&. 
.RE
.PP

